From: Monica Patel <monica.patel@redwood.ai>
To: Raf Mendes <rafael.mendes@redwood.ai>, Grace O'Connor <grace.oconnor@redwood.ai>, Vivek Kulkarni <vivek.kulkarni@redwood.ai>; Cleo Harris <cleo@parklane.co>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 08:18:00 -07:00
Subject: Re: [Action] Edge adapter warmup & cutover window proposal

Cleo / team — putting together the runbook now. Draft highlights below (I'll attach the full runbook to the calendar invite):

Pre-cutover (staging, 48-24h):
- Run warmup script in staging with model ids listed; collect KV hit ratio and JIT compilation counts. Target KV hit > 60% for search-v2.
- Smoke tests: 1000 small queries (50ms median) and 50 long tail queries; pass = p99 < 2.0s and error rate < 0.5%.
- Confirm fallback model (rerank-mini-quant) is present in the pool and tagged for immediate substitution.

Day-of commands (short examples):
- Warmup loop (curl):
  for i in {1..500}; do curl -s -X POST "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate?model=search-v2" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "X-Redwood-Warmup: 1" -d '{"prompt": "find: coffee near A"}'; sleep 0.12; done

- Node prefetch example (from samples):
  const prewarm = async (client, payloads) => {
    for (const p of payloads) {
      try {
        await client.generate({model: 'search-v2', input: p, headers: {'X-Redwood-Warmup': '1'}});
      } catch (e) {
        // stop if series of 5xx errors detected
        throw e;
      }
    }
  }

Retries and timeouts recommended: client timeout 8s, connect timeout 1s, 3 retries with full-jitter backoff (base 250ms).

Sign-offs needed before schedule:
- Parklane infra OK on window and fallback DNS routing.
- Redwood eng confirm fallback model slots (Vivek).
- Security: ensure warmup requests flagged so they are not counted towards billing (Raf: already requested).

I'll drop the runbook doc into the drive link and send the invite once Jermaine confirms.

- Monica
Senior Implementation Manager — Redwood Inference
